# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
*.egg-info/

# Tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
# The code graph (arch-a): 28 MB of derived AST, rebuilt from the repo by the post-commit
# hook after every commit. Committing it would carry an 11 MB churn diff per commit and the
# committed copy would always be one async rebuild behind the tree it claims to describe.
graphify-out/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Secrets and Telegram session state (docs/SPEC.md §2)
.env
*.session
*.session-journal

# Vault runtime state (regenerated by the Stop hook)
knowledge/.vault-state.json
.obsidian/

# Raw / derived data and model weights never go into git — except the curated,
# frozen train/test splits, which are deliverables (docs/frozen-testsets.md).
data/*
!data/frozen/
# The draft category lexicon (4.5h): hand-written keyword stems, not collected data,
# and the only thing results/categories_45h.json can be re-derived from. It is marked
# `draft-not-law` in its own body — the taxonomy is the operator's word later.
!data/category_lexicon_draft.json
# Same reason for the hand-labelled sarcasm pool: it is annotation output that
# feeds training, not collected data (docs/frozen-testsets.md).
!data/annotation/
data/annotation/*
!data/annotation/sarcasm_candidates.jsonl
!data/annotation/sarcasm_holdout_pool.jsonl
# The taxonomy-v2 copies staged beside them (4.5e). Same kind of artifact as the
# file they were derived from, and useless to a reader who cannot diff the two.
!data/annotation/*_tax2.jsonl
# The pool at 917 rows (4.5h2): option (i) of the precheck, a NEW file beside the
# pristine 971 so that each of the 54 dual-home ids lives in exactly one place and
# the four records pinning the original's sha256 stay valid. Derived, and committed
# for the same reason its source is: the reader has to be able to diff the two.
!data/annotation/sarcasm_holdout_pool_v4.jsonl
# The up-label precheck (4.5g): 1,912 paid rows that a gate decision reads. Same
# rule as the line above — model output the operator calibrates, not collected
# data — and an artifact living only in a working tree is money spent twice.
!data/annotation/uplabel_precheck_45g.jsonl
# What a media-only post says (4.5g2): vision captions and poll transcripts. Same
# rule again — an input a labelling prompt reads, paid for once, and the images it
# was written from stay out (posts_media/ is data, and it is big).
!data/annotation/post_captions.jsonl
!data/annotation/uplabel_precheck_45g2.jsonl
# The second round (4.5g3): the same 1,912 rows re-labelled after all three strata came back
# under the bar. Same rule again, and the file the wave-2 gate pack is drawn from.
!data/annotation/uplabel_precheck_45g3.jsonl
# Generated, not collected — but the same kind of artifact: a curated training
# source, ablation-gated (knowledge/decisions/synthetic-sarcasm-augmentation.md).
!data/annotation/synthetic_sarcasm.jsonl
# What came back from the verdict sitting (4.5g3). Hand-made labels, not collected
# data, and a working tree is the only place they exist. A directory that is itself
# excluded cannot have a file re-included out of it, so each one is re-admitted and
# then re-emptied. The images stay out — posts_media/ is data, and it is big.
!data/annotation/sitting_45g/
data/annotation/sitting_45g/*
!data/annotation/sitting_45g/check20_blind.csv
!data/annotation/sitting_45g/emptied_redo.csv
!data/annotation/calib_45e/
data/annotation/calib_45e/*
!data/annotation/calib_45e/unreadable14.csv
# The sku-a text pack (SPEC 3.17 (6), bar 3): 30 pre-filtered rows the operator ticks by hand.
# Same rule as unreadable14.csv above and the same reason — an adjudication that exists only in a
# working tree is an evening nobody can restore, and `build_sku_text_pack.py --force` would take it
# with no HEAD behind it. The README goes in beside it because the pack is unreadable without the
# instructions it was filled in under.
!data/annotation/sku_a_text/
data/annotation/sku_a_text/*
!data/annotation/sku_a_text/text30.csv
!data/annotation/sku_a_text/README-text30.md
models/
*.safetensors
*.gguf
# Phase 4c syncs each arm's checkpoint home continuously (nothing may exist only
# on a pod), so the 250 MB optimizer state lands in the working tree. It is a
# resume artifact, not a deliverable; the adapter beside it is already covered by
# *.safetensors, and adapter_config.json / loss.jsonl / provenance.json are the
# small files that do get committed.
*.pt

# The aggregate layer (SPEC 3.20 (2)): rebuilt from data/derived/ by scripts/build_aggregates.py
# in about a second, and it holds no fact its inputs do not. `data/*` above already covers it —
# the entry is here because the DB is the one derived file a reader might expect to be committed,
# and because what ships is results/dashboard_data_w1.json, not this.
data/derived/pulse.db

# smoke runs write a record shaped exactly like a real one — same shape, fake numbers
results/smoke/

# the overnight XLM-R baseline writes here; the record it produces goes to results/
xlmr_full_run.log

# The suite stamp (scripts/baselines.py): what pytest last ran, in THIS working tree.
.suite-stamp.json

# The tick's own state (scripts/tick.py): when the last tick ran, what it wrote, what the schedule
# said. A clock, so committing it would dirty the tree on every `make tick` — and the phase's own
# check (l) asks `git status --porcelain results` to print nothing. The screen's fuel beside it,
# `results/promo_screen_data.json`, has no clock and IS committed.
results/promo_tick.json

# The loop daemon's wake log (scripts/loop_daemon.py, and launchd's copy of its streams under
# ops/com.marketpulse.loop.plist). A clock like the tick's state beside it: one line per wake, so
# committing it would dirty the tree every hour the operator leaves `make loop` running.
results/loop*.log
.claude/session_mode

# The front end's dependencies and its build (PHASE-ship-1 §2 front-1). `frontend/package.json` and
# `frontend/package-lock.json` ARE committed — `npm ci` installs exactly what was measured here —
# and `dashboard/app/` is what `make front` writes from them: a build output like the derived store
# above, so a clone builds it rather than carrying two copies of the same JSON. The operator's
# `firebase deploy` runs after `make front`, which is also what keeps §8's porcelain empty.
frontend/node_modules/
dashboard/app/

# The operator's own Firebase project id (`firebase use --add` writes it). `.firebaserc.example`
# IS committed and carries a placeholder: the hosting config in `firebase.json` is the product's,
# the project it deploys to is his. The executor never runs a deploy (PHASE-ship-1 §4.1).
.firebaserc
